LaTeX is widely used in academia for the communication and publication of scientific documents and technical note-taking in many fields, owing particularly to its support for complex mathematical notation, etc.

\subsection{Typesetting}

LaTeX attempts to follow the design philosophy of separation of presentation from content, so that authors can focus on the content of what they are writing without attending simultaneously to its visual appearance.

\subsection{Document}

To create a document in LaTeX, a user first creates a file, such as \texttt{document.tex}, typically using a text editor. The user then gives their \texttt{document.tex} file as input to the TeX program, which prompts TeX to write out a file suitable for onscreen viewing or printing.

